**What I found and fixed:** In `strip_ansi_codes` (`src/format/output.rs`), the CSI parameter-byte skip loop covered every byte in the ECMA-48 parameter range 0x30–0x3F **except** `:` (0x3A). Colon-separated SGR subparameters (ITU-T T.416 extended color, e.g. `ESC[38:2::255:0:0m` — emitted by terminals/tools) therefore leaked their `:` bytes into cleaned tool output as literal text — the same leak class fixed in the previous session for FE (ESC 7/8/=/=) and 3-char escapes. The fix adds `:` to the skip set (and moves `!` out of the parameter loop to the intermediate-byte loop where it belongs — behavior unchanged), plus a regression test.

